the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
*a creature* flies.
*a creature* is a parent of *a dragon*.
*a creature* is happy.
*a creature* is green.

the knowledge base flying_dragon includes:

a dragon flies if 
an other dragon is a parent of the dragon
and the other dragon flies
and the other dragon is green.


% a little hack: we add a first "is a" body condition to bind dragons...
% ... because the "for all cases..." does not bind the dragon variable, and our type checking (on unbound argument *a dragon*) is lazy
A dragon is happy if
	the dragon is a dragon and
    for all cases in which 
	    the dragon is a parent of an other dragon
		it is the case that 
		the other dragon flies.

scenario colourless is:
	bob is a dragon.
	alice is a dragon.
	alice is a parent of bob.

scenario green is:
	bob is a dragon.
	alice is a dragon.
	alice is a parent of bob.
	alice is green.
	alice flies.
	happy expects answers ["bob is happy","alice is happy"].
    
query happy is:
	which creature is happy.

query green is:
	which creature is green.
